{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4d7a9dd695bcb2a","type":"tool_result","content":"24:Authentication follows a two-layer model: kube-rbac-proxy fronts the Node.js backend (port 8443) performing OpenShift OAuth validation and injecting identity headers (`x-forwarded-access-token`, `x-auth-request-user`, `x-auth-request-groups`), while each Go BFF sidecar independently validates Bearer tokens and performs SubjectAccessReviews against the Kubernetes API for fine-grained authorization. The agent-ops BFF extends this with per-agent RBAC via SubjectAccessReviews for agent-specific access control. The Node.js backend additionally proxies Kubernetes API calls (`/api/k8s/*`) by converting user tokens to impersonation headers, allowing the frontend to interact with the cluster API through the dashboard service boundary. [source: backend/src/utils/constants.ts:18-20, backend/src/utils/proxy.ts:39-42, packages/agent-ops/bff/internal/api/middleware.go:1]\n351:| odh-dashboard-operator-role | opendatahub.io | odhdashboardconfigs | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n362:| odh-dashboard-operator-role | feast.dev | featurestores | get, list, watch |\n407:| dashboard-operator-role | opendatahub.io | odhdashboardconfigs | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n418:| dashboard-operator-role | feast.dev | featurestores | get, list, watch |\n456:| /api/k8s/* | ALL | Bearer Token to K8s Impersonation | Node.js proxy to K8s API | User Kubernetes RBAC |\n505:- **User request path:** Browser clients connect to the dashboard through an OpenShift Route that terminates TLS and forwards traffic to kube-rbac-proxy (port 8443). Kube-rbac-proxy validates the user's OpenShift OAuth token and injects identity headers (`x-forwarded-access-token`, `x-auth-request-user`, `x-auth-request-groups`) before forwarding to the Node.js Fastify backend. The backend serves the React SPA for UI requests at `/` and proxies `/api/k8s/*` requests to the Kubernetes API using user token impersonation. Module federation remotes are served at `/_mf/:name/*` paths, loading domain-specific UI bundles dynamically. [source: backend/src/utils/constants.ts:18-20, backend/src/utils/proxy.ts:39-42, backend/src/routes/root.ts:1, backend/src/routes/module-federation.ts:1]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79643b640be188f","agent_id":"af2e9536495148b77","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"07c95e52-2d8b-4033-aa4b-54959999274e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:14:01.718Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4d7a9dd695bcb2a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
