{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fa2c4d11-e348-4ba9-b623-53c51ec9e978","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89094ed77ff0bc66","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ozb06qk9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E001.md","content":"# Validate FeatureStore CRD schema and operator behavior for dashboard-driven admin CRUD\n\n## Description\n\nFeature Store Engineering validates the server-side assumptions the dashboard admin UI depends on, and resolves the open scope question that gates the create form wizard. The deliverable is a validated specification for the form: which FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) fields the TP create form exposes, their constraints and valid combinations, which backend combinations should be restricted, and written confirmation that the feast-operator correctly handles dashboard-created custom resources.\n\nThis epic also discharges the validation obligation owed on the feast-operator (a no-code-change component): confirming that CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources and that operator reconciliation is creation-method agnostic.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) OpenAPI schema and produce a field inventory for the create form: registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, TLS settings, scaling configuration, and materialization scheduling — each with type, required/optional status, constraints, defaults, and valid combinations.\n- Decide, with the PM and Feature Store engineering, whether the TP form exposes the full CRD spec or a curated subset, and record the rationale.\n- Identify backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (for example, SQLite as a development-only store unsuitable for production).\n- Confirm the feast-operator reconciles FeatureStore CRs created through the K8s API (dashboard path, not just kubectl), and that existing CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources — or document gaps and required remediation.\n- Confirm the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) is stable for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle, or escalate per the strategy risk.\n- Record CRD field mutability findings to inform any follow-on in-place editing iteration (out of scope for this strategy).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A field inventory document exists mapping each form-relevant FeatureStore CRD field to its type, required/optional status, constraints, and defaults, validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema.\n- A recorded decision (PM + Feature Store engineering) on TP form field scope — full CRD spec or curated subset — with rationale.\n- A list of restricted or discouraged backend combinations is produced for use as form validation rules.\n- Feature Store engineering confirms in writing that operator reconciliation and webhook validation cover dashboard-created CRs, or documents the gaps and remediation needed.\n- CRD stability for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle is confirmed, or an escalation is raised with the strategy owner.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Gates the P0 HLR \"deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard\" — the field set and validation constraints produced here determine what the wizard builds.\n- Informs the P2 HLR \"form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints\" (constraint inventory).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43394,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79643b640be188f","agent_id":"af2e9536495148b77","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"3a9cc335-5c61-4be4-b797-5920c03bec11","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:21:07.721Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
