{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fa2c4d11-e348-4ba9-b623-53c51ec9e978","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8deed1dc28880678","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ozb06qk9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E004.md","content":"# Feature Store create wizard in the RHOAI dashboard\n\n## Description\n\nBuild the guided create form wizard (React, PatternFly 6) in the odh-dashboard that lets a platform administrator deploy a new FeatureStore instance without YAML editing or CLI access. The wizard maps the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) spec to a step-by-step form and submits a valid custom resource to the K8s API through the dashboard's existing pass-through proxy, using the admin's own token.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Multi-step form wizard covering the TP field set decided with the PM and Feature Store engineering: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters.\n- Client-side validation derived from the FeatureStore CRD OpenAPI schema, with inline guidance for required fields, valid backend combinations, and scaling prerequisites; restricted or discouraged combinations (per the Feature Store validation deliverable) are flagged.\n- Submission via the existing K8s API pass-through (`/api/k8s/*`) — no new backend routes; RBAC enforcement happens at the K8s API level with the user's forwarded token.\n- Server-side validation feedback: if the K8s API rejects the submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the UI.\n- Air-gapped support: all form options and validation rules bundled in the dashboard's static assets; no external network fetches.\n- Feature-flag gating in OdhDashboardConfig so clusters without the Feature Store component see no UI change.\n- Reuse applicable prototype components (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) per the alignment assessment.\n- Admin-only access: write access enforced by the dashboard's admin-route middleware plus K8s RBAC.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The wizard renders all fields in the decided TP field set without error and submits a valid FeatureStore CR to the K8s API.\n- Inline validation guidance for CRD schema constraints is provided before submission (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites).\n- A K8s API rejection of the submitted CR is surfaced as an actionable error in the UI.\n- No form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access (air-gapped compatible).\n- The wizard is gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag; clusters without the Feast component show no UI change.\n- Create operations succeed at runtime once the expanded dashboard ClusterRole (feast.dev/featurestores write verbs) is applied — verified against a cluster with the RBAC manifest changes in place.\n- Form field mapping is validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time (mitigates CRD version drift).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard.\n- P1: admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n- P2: form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43394,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79643b640be188f","agent_id":"af2e9536495148b77","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"723a6d42-07ff-4c11-a6e6-73e9aafe82b7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:21:41.273Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007"}
