{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c8e49056-9b7a-4711-805e-8b442e33c312","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf8f7f3110d09f7b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-ozb06qk9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E005.md","content":"# Feature Store management pages (list, detail, delete, status tracking)\n\n## Description\n\nBuild the Feature Store management surface in the odh-dashboard: a list page showing all FeatureStore instances across the admin's accessible namespaces, a read-only detail/inspect view of the full custom resource spec and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation, and real-time deployment status tracking — all gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Management list page: one row per FeatureStore instance with name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp; actions to inspect and delete.\n- Real-time status: status polling using the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns so readiness state updates (Deploying → Ready) without manual refresh.\n- Read-only detail view: full FeatureStore CR spec (online/offline store backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, without truncation; links to the Feast UI Route for browsing feature metadata when available.\n- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a DELETE request to the K8s API via the existing pass-through proxy; the feast-operator handles owned-resource cleanup via finalizers.\n- Permission-aware UI: write controls (create button, delete action) hidden for non-admin (viewer) users based on the dashboard's existing admin status check; viewers keep list and detail access under the existing viewer ClusterRole.\n- Feature-flag gating in OdhDashboardConfig; no UI change on clusters without the Feast component.\n- Reuse applicable prototype components (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) per the alignment assessment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All FeatureStore instances in the admin's accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp — matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces.\n- Deployment status reflects `.status.conditions` of the FeatureStore CR within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from Deploying to Ready without manual refresh.\n- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions in read-only format, without truncation.\n- Delete with confirmation removes the FeatureStore CR via the K8s API; the instance disappears from the list and the operator cleans up owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, Routes).\n- Non-admin (viewer) users see the list and detail views with no create or delete controls.\n- List, detail, and delete operations succeed at runtime once the expanded dashboard ClusterRole (feast.dev/featurestores write verbs) is applied.\n- The pages are gated behind the feature flag; no new external network connections are introduced.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: view all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, and creation time.\n- P0: inspect the configuration of any FeatureStore instance in a read-only detail view.\n- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance from the dashboard with a confirmation dialog.\n- P0: deployment progress (readiness status) visible in the dashboard, updating in real time.\n- P1: non-admin users can browse instances but cannot create or delete them.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46112,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79643b640be188f","agent_id":"af2e9536495148b77","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"7716d0f4-39b8-40d3-8675-2a4eacedbfd3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:22:01.6