\t| CRD mutability / edit capability — open question | Editing is explicitly Out-of-Scope for this strategy; the answer does not change this strategy's epics. Captured as an informational output of E001 for the follow-on iteration. Not an epic. |\n102\t| UXD design timeline — open question | Scheduling/process unknown — does not change which epics exist. Health warning (E003 is on the critical path). |\n103\t| Performance targets for TP — open question | Does not change epic structure (admin CRUD is low-frequency per strategy). Health warning. |\n104\t| Admin RBAC permissions in target namespaces — needs-validation assumption | Resolved by doing E006 (the RBAC extension is the coverage); captured as an AC on E006. |\n105\t\n106\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n107\t\n108\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n109\t| --- | --- | --- |\n110\t| Deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) | P0 | E004 (built), gated by E001/E002, designed in E003, enabled at runtime by E006 |\n111\t| View all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, creation time | P0 | E005 |\n112\t| Inspect configuration of any instance in read-only detail view | P0 | E005 |\n113\t| Delete instance from dashboard with confirmation dialog | P0 | E005 (operator cleanup via finalizers) |\n114\t| Deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time | P0 | E005 |\n115\t| Non-admin (viewer) browse-only access | P1 | E005 (UI gating), E006 (K8s RBAC enforcement), E008 (validation) |\n116\t| Admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E004 (static bundling of options/validation/assets), E008 (air-gapped cluster validation) |\n117\t| Form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints | P2 | E004 — bundled: shares the wizard's form surface and validation model; not independently deferrable |\n118\t\n119\tAll HLRs covered; no orphans.\n120\t\n121\t## Health Warnings\n122\t\n123\t1. **P2 inline-validation HLR bundled into E004**: it shares the wizard's form surface and validation-rule model — splitting it would duplicate the form implementation. Not a deferrable feature split (Step 4).\n124\t2. **UXD timeline unscheduled** (`needs-uxd` queued, no design sprint scheduled): E003 sits on the critical path and gates both frontend epics; a UXD delay slips all P0 delivery. Strategy mitigation: use prototype PR #7013 as a starting design reference to unblock.\n125\t3. **Edit-capability contradiction**: \"editing an existing FeatureStore instance\" is both Out-of-Scope and an open question. Treated as out of scope per the strategy's explicit statement; CRD mutability findings are recorded in E001 for the follow-on.\n126\t4. **Performance targets undefined**: no perf epic created; if targets emerge they become ACs on the QE validation epic. Low-frequency admin access pattern per strategy.\n127\t5. **Strategy-level process gates pending**: Architecture Review and Documentation Support are \"Pending human review\" in Prerequisites — outside decomposition control; flagged so a human confirms them.\n128\t6. **feast-operator ClusterRole naming**: strategy references `featurestore-editor-role`/`featurestore-viewer-role`; architecture context also shows `feast-operator-featurestore-editor-role` variants — E006 must reference the role actually bound in the target namespace (AC on E006).\n129\t\n130\t## Tiered Delivery\n131\t\n132\tNot applicable. No external dependency with uncertain timing (PatternFly 6 v6.4.x already in odh-dashboard; CRD and operator already shipped in RHOAI 3.5-ea.1). All internal dependencies exist.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd6244da8d595585","agent_id":"a5e132a7373d8439d","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"ecb896a1-9691-4d79-95ac-72f2b94e363e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:26:39.472Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4c6842228a6d959","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","s