{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ae60ee303e10f75","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate FeatureStore CRD schema and operator behavior for dashboard-driven\n4\t  admin CRUD\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: Feature Store\n7\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate FeatureStore CRD schema and operator behavior for dashboard-driven admin CRUD\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tFeature Store Engineering validates the server-side assumptions the dashboard admin UI depends on, and resolves the open scope question that gates the create form wizard. The deliverable is a validated specification for the form: which FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) fields the TP create form exposes, their constraints and valid combinations, which backend combinations should be restricted, and written confirmation that the feast-operator correctly handles dashboard-created custom resources.\n31\t\n32\tThis epic also discharges the validation obligation owed on the feast-operator (a no-code-change component): confirming that CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources and that operator reconciliation is creation-method agnostic.\n33\t\n34\t## Scope\n35\t\n36\t- Analyze the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) OpenAPI schema and produce a field inventory for the create form: registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, TLS settings, scaling configuration, and materialization scheduling — each with type, required/optional status, constraints, defaults, and valid combinations.\n37\t- Decide, with the PM and Feature Store engineering, whether the TP form exposes the full CRD spec or a curated subset, and record the rationale.\n38\t- Identify backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (for example, SQLite as a development-only store unsuitable for production).\n39\t- Confirm the feast-operator reconciles FeatureStore CRs created through the K8s API (dashboard path, not just kubectl), and that existing CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources — or document gaps and required remediation.\n40\t- Confirm the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) is stable for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle, or escalate per the strategy risk.\n41\t- Record CRD field mutability findings to inform any follow-on in-place editing iteration (out of scope for this strategy).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A field inventory document exists mapping each form-relevant FeatureStore CRD field to its type, required/optional status, constraints, and defaults, validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema.\n46\t- A recorded decision (PM + Feature Store engineering) on TP form field scope — full CRD spec or curated subset — with rationale.\n47\t- A list of restricted or discouraged backend combinations is produced for use as form validation rules.\n48\t- Feature Store engineering confirms in writing that operator reconciliation and webhook validation cover dashboard-created CRs, or documents the gaps and remediation needed.\n49\t- CRD stability for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle is confirmed, or an escalation is raised with the strategy owner.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- Gates the P0 HLR \"deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard\" — the field set and validation constraints produced here determine what the wizard builds.\n54\t- Informs the P2 HLR \"form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints\" (constraint inventory).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd6244da8d595585","agent_id":"a5e132a7373d8439d","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"07bdee79-b15f-49f2-8f7e-1c15c4274218","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:26:45.061Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ae60ee303e10f75","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
