{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91354f347b9a183d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the strategy approach'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the strategy approach\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDashboard Engineering, with Feature Store Engineering consultation, determines how much of the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) can be reused for the formal implementation of the Feature Store admin UI, and whether the prototype's architecture matches the strategy's approach — K8s API pass-through for CRUD, the existing read proxy for Feast Registry data, admin-route gating, and feature-flag rollout.\n30\t\n31\tThe outcome determines whether the frontend implementation starts from reworked prototype code or from scratch, so it must be resolved before the admin UI pages are built.\n32\t\n33\t## Scope\n34\t\n35\t- Review the prototype PR code against the strategy's technical approach: RBAC usage, API routes (`/api/k8s/*` pass-through for CRUD, existing read proxy for instance metadata), page structure, and feature gating.\n36\t- Identify which prototype components (create wizard, list page, detail view, delete flow) are reusable, and where the prototype diverges from the formal path (PatternFly 6 usage, CRD spec coverage, air-gapped constraints, feature-flag gating).\n37\t- Produce a reuse plan per admin UI surface — what to carry over, what to rebuild — confirmed with Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A written assessment documents where the prototype aligns with and diverges from the strategy approach, per admin UI surface.\n42\t- A reuse recommendation per surface (create wizard, list page, detail view, delete flow) is produced and confirmed with the Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Gates all P0 admin UI HLRs (create wizard, list, inspect, delete, status tracking) — the reuse determination changes the implementation approach for the frontend work.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd6244da8d595585","agent_id":"a5e132a7373d8439d","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"488e0928-bfe5-4e79-9902-7de0bce6eeac","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:26:46.155Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91354f347b9a183d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
