{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7ef970bd4010367","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n3\ttitle: Dashboard RBAC extension and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin\n4\t  CRUD\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard RBAC extension and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tExtend the odh-dashboard's Kubernetes RBAC and deploy-time configuration so platform administrators can create, update, patch, and delete FeatureStore custom resources through the dashboard, and so the new admin UI can be rolled out progressively behind a feature flag. This is a manifest-and-configuration change — no new backend routes or BFF modules.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Extend the dashboard ClusterRole (`manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml`) with `create, update, patch, delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores`, preserving existing `get, list, watch`. Use the feast-operator's editor ClusterRole as the reference for the minimum permission set; reference the role variant actually bound in target namespaces.\n39\t- Add the Feature Store admin UI feature flag default to OdhDashboardConfig for progressive rollout.\n40\t- Verify that platform administrators hold `feast.dev/featurestores` write verbs in target namespaces once the extension is applied (a needs-validation assumption in the strategy).\n41\t- Confirm the two-tier authorization model: admin writes enforced at the K8s API level via the user's forwarded token through kube-rbac-proxy, plus the dashboard's admin-route middleware check; viewer users unchanged (read-only via the existing viewer ClusterRole).\n42\t- Preserve security posture: TLS 1.2+ via service-ca, no new external network connections, FIPS compliance unchanged (manifest-only changes, no new Go BFF module).\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- The dashboard ClusterRole grants `create, update, patch, delete` (in addition to existing `get, list, watch`) for `feast.dev/featurestores`.\n47\t- Admin users can create and delete FeatureStore CRs through the dashboard's K8s API pass-through; non-admin users without the editor role binding cannot write FeatureStore CRs regardless of UI state (enforcement is at the K8s API, not only UI hiding).\n48\t- Viewer permissions are unchanged: `get, list, watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status` only.\n49\t- The feature flag default lands per the rollout plan; clusters without the Feast component enabled see no dashboard changes.\n50\t- No new external network connections; existing TLS and FIPS posture is preserved.\n51\t- Rollback: reverting the manifest restores the prior RBAC state with no data migration (backwards compatible — no changes to the Feast CRD schema or operator behavior).\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for deploying (create) and deleting FeatureStore instances from the dashboard.\n56\t- Covers the enforcement side of the P1 viewer read-only HLR (K8s RBAC tier).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd6244da8d595585","agent_id":"a5e132a7373d8439d","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"1a45e47e-f09e-46e5-98a0-1d91d8da9417","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:26:58.038Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7ef970bd40