trategy. (Arithmetic/thresholds not checked — computed by pipeline.)\n58\t\n59\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n60\t\n61\tEvery epic has testable, strategy-derived ACs. Rule-mandated ACs are present where applicable: E006 (the replacement/config epic) has both a rollback AC (\"reverting the manifest restores the prior RBAC state\") and feature-flag rollout ACs; E004 and E005 each have feature-flag gating ACs; E007 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC (\"technically reviewed against the implemented UI by engineering before publication\"). No konflux chain exists, so the build-pipeline AC is not applicable. ACs are measurable (e.g., list matching `kubectl get featurestores -A`, status reflecting `.status.conditions` within the watch/poll cycle, `kubectl get featurestore <name>` returning NotFound after delete, air-gapped deployment with no external connectivity). No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — dependencies are described in plain terms (\"per the alignment assessment\", \"the Feature Store validation deliverable\").\n62\t\n63\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n64\t\n65\tAll strategy scope is covered: every RFE acceptance criterion (wizard, deploying→ready status, list, detail, delete+cleanup, viewer read-only, air-gapped) maps to epic scope/ACs; the RBAC extension, feature flag, UXD design obligation, documentation, and QE validation each have a dedicated epic. Cross-epic completeness holds — the multi-item upstream scopes (CRD field groups, wizard/detail surfaces) are all accounted for in E004/E005. Strategy-level context is carried forward rather than dropped: all six risks map to concrete mitigations in epics (UXD delay → prototype as design reference in E003; CRD drift → build-time schema validation AC in E004; air-gapped validation gaps → server-side error surfacing AC in E004; pod resource growth → E008 AC; viewer RBAC bypass → E006/E008 enforcement ACs); every needs-validation assumption and open question has an explicit disposition in the Investigation Decisions table. Out-of-scope items (editing, multi-tenant, permissions UI, RHAISTRAT-7215 scope) are correctly excluded, with the edit-capability contradiction resolved and documented. The Documentation Support prerequisite is \"Pending human review\" (not a plain \"Yes\"), and a docs-authoring epic (E007) exists regardless. The bounded field-scope outcome is modeled as `gated_by` + `rewrite` rather than branch files, with justification that epic structure is unchanged either way — acceptable, and no branch files were created, so no branch-coverage gap exists.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af9f54f7f25fdefb","agent_id":"a2027bdfb39992f71","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"79dd366f-6e31-4754-80e3-4c02b80be93a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:35:12.288Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ace39217ffe8aa6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
