{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f2d9f1158789d5b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007\n11\t\n12\tFeature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy is M-effort (3-5 sprints), spans multiple work streams (React frontend pages, RBAC/manifest backend changes, UXD design authoring, QE validation, documentation), and contains genuine open questions that gate downstream scope (TP form field set, prototype alignment). Not docs-only: code changes in odh-dashboard. Full decomposition proceeds.\n17\t\n18\t**Staff Engineer Input**: section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to log.\n19\t\n20\t## Component Mapping Notes\n21\t\n22\tCanonical component names from `.context/rhai-components.txt` (the strategy's names are mapped to the closest canonical entry):\n23\t\n24\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n25\t| --- | --- | --- |\n26\t| odh-dashboard (frontend / backend / manifests) | AI Core Dashboard | No literal `odh-dashboard` entry in the canonical list; AI Core Dashboard is the closest canonical match for the RHOAI dashboard |\n27\t| feast-operator | Feature Store | Passive component — no code changes expected; validated by a different team (Feature Store Engineering), so per Step 2 exception it gets its own Investigation epic |\n28\t| UXD design assets | UXD | |\n29\t| Admin guides | Documentation | |\n30\t| Test suites | QE | |\n31\t\n32\tBoth odh-dashboard and feast have architecture context files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-dashboard.md`, `feast.md`) — no onboarding chain (Rule 20) is needed. The strategy's architecture claims were spot-checked and hold: `featurestore-editor-role`/`featurestore-viewer-role` exist in `feast.md` RBAC section; `/api/k8s/*` impersonation proxy and `feast.dev/featurestores` read verbs in the dashboard ClusterRole are confirmed in `odh-dashboard.md`.\n33\t\n34\t## Epic List\n35\t\n36\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n37\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Validate FeatureStore CRD schema and operator behavior for dashboard-driven admin CRUD | Investigation | Feature Store Engineering | P0 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 | Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the strategy approach | Investigation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 | UXD wireframes and interaction patterns for the Feature Store admin UI | Implementation | UXD Team | P0 |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 | Feature Store create wizard in the RHOAI dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 | Feature Store management pages (list, detail, delete, status tracking) | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 | Dashboard RBAC extension and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 | Admin guide documentation for the Feature Store admin UI | Implementation | Documentation Team | P1 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 | QE validation of the Feature Store admin UI (CRUD, RBAC tiers, air-gapped) | Implementation | QE Team | P1 |\n46\t\n47\t## Dependency DAG\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 CRD schema and operator validation]\n52\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 prototype alignment assessment]\n53\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 UXD wireframes]\n54\t    E004[RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 create wizard]\n55\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 management pages]\n56\t    E006[RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 RBAC and feature-flag manifests]\n57\t    E007[RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 admin guide docs]\n58\t    E008[RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 QE validation]\n59\t    E001 --> E003\n60\t    E001 --> E004\n61\t    E002 --> E004\n62\t    E002 --> E005\n63\t    E003 --> E004\n64\t    E003 --> E005\n65\t    E004 --> E007\n66\t    E005 --> E007\n67\t    E006 --> E007\n68\t    E004 --> E008\n69\t    E005 --> E008\n70\t    E006 --> E008\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\tCritical path: E001 → E003 → E004 → E007/E008 (length 4).\n74\t\n75\t## DAG Justification\n76\t\n77\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n78\t| --- | --- | --- |\n79\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The TP form field set (full CRD spec vs curated subset) and backend-combination restrictions are inputs to the wizard wireframes; the design cannot be finalized without them. True gate: `rewrite` of design scope. |\n80\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | The validated CRD field inventory, constraints, and restricted backend combinations determine what the wizard form builds. True gate: `rewrite`. Bounded outcome (curated subset vs full spec) changes wizard scope, not epic structure, so no branch files — recorded as `gate_failure_impact` on E004. |\n81\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 3 | Prototype alignment determines how much of PR #7013 is reused vs rebuilt — changes the implementation approach. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n82\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 | Same prototype-reuse determination applies to the list/detail/delete surfaces. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n83\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 12 (artifact producer → consumer) | Strategy dependency table: form wizard designs are required before implementation; the wizard builds against the approved wireframes. |\n84\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 12 | Management page (list/detail) designs required before implementation, per the same dependency. |\n85\t| E006 ∥ E004, E006 ∥ E005 | Rules 13/15 (no edge) | The RBAC ClusterRole extension and feature flag are manifest/configuration changes — not artifacts the frontend code builds against. Coupling is enforced by ACs on E004/E005 (\"CRUD succeeds at runtime with the expanded ClusterRole\"), never by a DAG edge. Same repo, different areas → parallel. |\n86\t| E004 ∥ E005 | Rule 15 | Same repo and team, but distinct UI surfaces (create form wizard vs management views) — split for scoped PR review cycles, run in parallel. They share the FeatureStore CR data available via existing proxies, not a co-built structure. |\n87\t| E004/E005/E006 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic blocked by all Implementation epics that build the feature; docs describe what was built. Docs priority exception applies (Major → P1; no priority inheritance). |\n88\t| E004/E005/E006 → E008 | Rule 12 (consumer of built artifact) | QE cross-team validation exercises the finished UI surfaces plus RBAC manifests together (CRUD flows, admin vs viewer enforcement, air-gapped) — requires all three implementation epics complete. |\n89\t\n90\t## Investigation Decisions (Step 3 scan)\n91\t\n92\tUnknowns scanned across open questions, risks, assumptions, and prerequisites. Disposition:\n93\t\n94\t| Unknown | Disposition |\n95\t| --- | --- |\n96\t| TP form field scope (full CRD vs curated subset) — open question, PM + FS Eng | Investigation E001 (changes what the wizard and wireframes build). Bounded (2 outcomes) but both keep the same epic structure — modeled as `gated_by` + `rewrite`, not branch files. |\n97\t| Restricted backend combinations (SQLite dev-only) — open question | Folded into E001 deliverable (informs form validation rules). |\n98\t| Prototype PR #7013 alignment — open question + needs-validation assumption | Investigation E002 (changes implementation approach for both frontend epics). |\n99\t| FeatureStore CRD stability in 3.5 cycle — needs-validation assumption | Folded into E001 (confirm or escalate). |\n100\t| Operator reconciliation of dashboard-created CRs / webhook validation sufficiency — feast-operator affected-components row | Folded into E001 (this is the passive-component validation owed by Feature Store Engineering). |\n101\t| CRD mutability / edit capability — open question | Editing is explicitly Out-of-Scope for this strategy; the answer does not change this strategy's epics. Captured as an informational output of E001 for the follow-on iteration. Not an epic. |\n102\t| UXD design timeline — open question | Scheduling/process unknown — does not change which epics exist. Health warning (E003 is on the critical path). |\n103\t| Performance targets for TP — open question | Does not change epic structure (admin CRUD is low-frequency per strategy). Health warning. |\n104\t| Admin RBAC permissions in target namespaces — needs-validation assumption | Resolved by doing E006 (the RBAC extension is the coverage); captured as an AC on E006. |\n105\t\n106\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n107\t\n108\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n109\t| --- | --- | --- |\n110\t| Deploy new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backend, authorization mode, scaling) | P0 | E004 (built), gated by E001/E002, designed in E003, enabled at runtime by E006 |\n111\t| View all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, creation time | P0 | E005 |\n112\t| Inspect configuration of any instance in read-only detail view | P0 | E005 |\n113\t| Delete instance from dashboard with confirmation dialog | P0 | E005 (operator cleanup via finalizers) |\n114\t| Deployment progress / readiness status visible in real time | P0 | E005 |\n115\t| Non-admin (viewer) browse-only access | P1 | E005 (UI gating), E006 (K8s RBAC enforcement), E008 (validation) |\n116\t| Admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E004 (static bundling of options/validation/assets), E008 (air-gapped cluster validation) |\n117\t| Form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints | P2 | E004 — bundled: shares the wizard's form surface and validation model; not independently deferrable |\n118\t\n119\tAll HLRs covered; no orphans.\n120\t\n121\t## Health Warnings\n122\t\n123\t1. **P2 inline-validation HLR bundled into E004**: it shares the wizard's form surface and validation-rule model — splitting it would duplicate the form implementation. Not a deferrable feature split (Step 4).\n124\t2. **UXD timeline unscheduled** (`needs-uxd` queued, no design sprint scheduled): E003 sits on the critical path and gates both frontend epics; a UXD delay slips all P0 delivery. Strategy mitigation: use prototype PR #7013 as a starting design reference to unblock.\n125\t3. **Edit-capability contradiction**: \"editing an existing FeatureStore instance\" is both Out-of-Scope and an open question. Treated as out of scope per the strategy's explicit statement; CRD mutability findings are recorded in E001 for the follow-on.\n126\t4. **Performance targets undefined**: no perf epic created; if targets emerge they become ACs on the QE validation epic. Low-frequency admin access pattern per strategy.\n127\t5. **Strategy-level process gates pending**: Architecture Review and Documentation Support are \"Pending human review\" in Prerequisites — outside decomposition control; flagged so a human confirms them.\n128\t6. **feast-operator ClusterRole naming**: strategy references `featurestore-editor-role`/`featurestore-viewer-role`; architecture context also shows `feast-operator-featurestore-editor-role` variants — E006 must reference the role actually bound in the target namespace (AC on E006).\n129\t\n130\t## Tiered Delivery\n131\t\n132\tNot applicable. No external dependency with uncertain timing (PatternFly 6 v6.4.x already in odh-dashboard; CRD and operator already shipped in RHOAI 3.5-ea.1). All internal dependencies exist.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfe51b71a3ec8f6","agent_id":"a8179d2dd99a8dd90","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"5816739f-ee82-4245-be7b-f4391b8f980e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:38:54.940Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f2d9f1158789d5b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","so