 validation guidance presentation.\n44\t- Wireframes for the management list page: instance rows with name, namespace, deployment status, creation timestamp, and actions (inspect, delete).\n45\t- Wireframes for the read-only detail view: configured backends, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule, and deployment conditions.\n46\t- Interaction patterns for the delete confirmation dialog, real-time status updates (deploying → ready), and error surfacing when the K8s API rejects a submission.\n47\t- Admin vs viewer (non-admin) variants: viewer users see list and detail views without create/delete controls.\n48\t- Designs must respect air-gapped constraints — no external assets or network-fetched resources.\n49\t- Use the engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as a starting design reference to unblock progress, per the strategy risk mitigation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Wireframes and interaction patterns for the create wizard, list page, and detail view are delivered and pass design review.\n54\t- Designs reflect the TP form field set decided with the PM and Feature Store engineering.\n55\t- Viewer (non-admin) read-only variants are documented, with write controls absent.\n56\t- Delete confirmation and real-time status interaction patterns are specified.\n57\t- Designs require no external network resources (air-gapped compatible).\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- Enables the P0 HLRs for the create wizard, list page, detail view, and delete flow (designs are prerequisites to implementation).\n62\t- Covers the user-facing aspect of the P1 viewer read-only HLR.\n63\t- Shapes the P2 inline validation guidance HLR.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfe51b71a3ec8f6","agent_id":"a8179d2dd99a8dd90","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"61254b0e-1c20-4290-8e48-aa15d2ccbce5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:39:14.089Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3ad12d2c8