{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-954c0a160d32347f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: Feature Store create wizard in the RHOAI dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001,RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'Gate RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 (CRD schema and TP field-scope validation):\n17\t    if the schema is unstable or the field-scope decision diverges from the assumed\n18\t    full-spec form, the wizards field set, validation rules, and form structure are\n19\t    rewritten to the validated field inventory. Gate RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 (prototype\n20\t    alignment assessment): if PR #7013 diverges from the strategy approach, the implementation\n21\t    is rebuilt from established dashboard patterns instead of prototype code.'\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 1\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n26\t  existing_foundation: 1\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 0\n29\t  human_process_gates: -1\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: High\n35\tai_implementability_score: 4\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\tbranch: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Feature Store create wizard in the RHOAI dashboard\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tBuild the guided create form wizard (React, PatternFly 6) in the odh-dashboard that lets a platform administrator deploy a new FeatureStore instance without YAML editing or CLI access. The wizard maps the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1) spec to a step-by-step form and submits a valid custom resource to the K8s API through the dashboard's existing pass-through proxy, using the admin's own token.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Multi-step form wizard covering the TP field set decided with the PM and Feature Store engineering: namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters.\n48\t- Client-side validation derived from the FeatureStore CRD OpenAPI schema, with inline guidance for required fields, valid backend combinations, and scaling prerequisites; restricted or discouraged combinations (per the Feature Store validation deliverable) are flagged.\n49\t- Submission via the existing K8s API pass-through (`/api/k8s/*`) — no new backend routes; RBAC enforcement happens at the K8s API level with the user's forwarded token.\n50\t- Server-side validation feedback: if the K8s API rejects the submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the UI.\n51\t- Air-gapped support: all form options and validation rules bundled in the dashboard's static assets; no external network fetches.\n52\t- Feature-flag gating in OdhDashboardConfig so clusters without the Feature Store component see no UI change.\n53\t- Reuse applicable prototype components (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) per the alignment assessment.\n54\t- Admin-only access: write access enforced by the dashboard's admin-route middleware plus K8s RBAC.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The wizard renders all fields in the decided TP field set without error and submits a valid FeatureStore CR to the K8s API.\n59\t- Inline validation guidance for CRD schema constraints is provided before submission (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites).\n60\t- A K8s API rejection of the submitted CR is surfaced as an actionable error in the UI.\n61\t- No form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access (air-gapped compatible).\n62\t- The wizard is gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag; clusters without the Feast component show no UI change.\n63\t- Create operations succeed at runtime once the expanded dashboard ClusterRole (feast.dev/featurestores write verbs) is applied — verified against a cluster with the RBAC manifest changes in place.\n64\t- Form field mapping is validated against the CRD OpenAPI schema at build time (mitigates CRD version drift).\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- P0: deploy a new FeatureStore instance from the dashboard via a guided form wizard.\n69\t- P1: admin UI functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n70\t- P2: form validation provides inline guidance for CRD schema constraints.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfe51b71a3ec8f6","agent_id":"a8179d2dd99a8dd90","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"5499f571-d2ee-4aef-84c2-250615bf8bbb","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:39:15.125Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-954c0a160d32347f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
