{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a82df94e988d7a77","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Feature Store management pages (list, detail, delete, status tracking)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If the prototype alignment assessment finds PR #7013 diverges\n16\t    from the strategy approach, the list/detail/delete surfaces are rebuilt from established\n17\t    dashboard patterns instead of reworked prototype code.'\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Feature Store management pages (list, detail, delete, status tracking)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBuild the Feature Store management surface in the odh-dashboard: a list page showing all FeatureStore instances across the admin's accessible namespaces, a read-only detail/inspect view of the full custom resource spec and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation, and real-time deployment status tracking — all gated behind the OdhDashboardConfig feature flag.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Management list page: one row per FeatureStore instance with name, namespace, deployment status (from `.status.conditions`), and creation timestamp; actions to inspect and delete.\n44\t- Real-time status: status polling using the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns so readiness state updates (Deploying → Ready) without manual refresh.\n45\t- Read-only detail view: full FeatureStore CR spec (online/offline store backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling settings, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, without truncation; links to the Feast UI Route for browsing feature metadata when available.\n46\t- Delete flow: confirmation dialog, then a DELETE request to the K8s API via the existing pass-through proxy; the feast-operator handles owned-resource cleanup via finalizers.\n47\t- Permission-aware UI: write controls (create button, delete action) hidden for non-admin (viewer) users based on the dashboard's existing admin status check; viewers keep list and detail access under the existing viewer ClusterRole.\n48\t- Feature-flag gating in OdhDashboardConfig; no UI change on clusters without the Feast component.\n49\t- Reuse applicable prototype components (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) per the alignment assessment.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- All FeatureStore instances in the admin's accessible namespaces are listed with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp — matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` for those namespaces.\n54\t- Deployment status reflects `.status.conditions` of the FeatureStore CR within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle, updating from Deploying to Ready without manual refresh.\n55\t- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions in read-only format, without truncation.\n56\t- Delete with confirmation removes the FeatureStore CR via the K8s API; the instance disappears from the list and the operator cleans up owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, Routes).\n57\t- Non-admin (viewer) users see the list and detail views with no create or delete controls.\n58\t- List, detail, and delete operations succeed at runtime once the expanded dashboard ClusterRole (feast.dev/featurestores write verbs) is applied.\n59\t- The pages are gated behind the feature flag; no new external network connections are introduced.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- P0: view all FeatureStore instances with name, namespace, status, and creation time.\n64\t- P0: inspect the configuration of any FeatureStore instance in a read-only detail view.\n65\t- P0: delete a FeatureStore instance from the dashboard with a confirmation dialog.\n66\t- P0: deployment progress (readiness status) visible in the dashboard, updating in real time.\n67\t- P1: non-admin users can browse instances but cannot create or delete them.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bfe51b71a3ec8f6","agent_id":"a8179d2dd99a8dd90","session_id":"420e9024-f833-42df-9d31-a5dd457541d8","uuid":"054cee20-7223-4e3a-93be-8a43c43f9c59","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:39:32.911Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a82df94e988d7a77","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
